  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Wu Yuan Ju tells Rong Hao that Blood Tide Pit was not naturally formed and that Blood Sea Ancestor created it on purpose as one of the true inheritances he meticulously arranged. After a Shang clan Gu Master took a Blood Sea true inheritance there and obtained blood handprint Gu, blood tides began to appear in the pit without cease. Wu Du Xiu then sent Gu Immortals and made the pit part of Wu clan territory, and under Wu clan management it became a blood path resource point that contributed to the clan’s blood path development.",
      "chapters": [
        1339
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_blood_sea_ancestor",
        "fac_shang_clan",
        "sys_gu_master",
        "inh_blood_sea_true_inheritance",
        "gu_blood_handprint_gu",
        "char_wu_du_xiu",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_wu_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Wu Yi Ran died, Blood Tide Pit was taken down and the Gu formations inside were destroyed, so the blood tide burst out and flooded the surrounding area across more than ten mountains. Wu Yuan Ju and Rong Hao pushed the tide back into the pit to seal it again, and Purple Mountain True Monarch later looked over the pit while controlling the scene there.",
      "chapters": [
        1339
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blood-flood",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_formation",
        "char_purple_mountain_true_monarch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration states that Blood Tide Pit contained a true inheritance of Blood Sea Ancestor, obtained by mortal Gu Master Shang Yan Fei and later taken by Wu clan, which explored it, found nothing special beyond the resource point use, and held it as a possession. When Wu Yong and others return, a breeding ground of blood beasts rises from the pit, including desolate level and ancient blood beasts born from natural blood path dao marks. After Wu Yong destroys those beasts, the blood tide dries out and the dense blood path dao marks vanish, so Blood Tide Pit no longer exists as that resource and is only an ordinary pit.",
      "chapters": [
        1341
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blood-beasts-and-drying",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shang_yan_fei",
        "char_wu_yong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu clan’s Blood Tide Pit produced more profits than Fang Yuan’s dragonfish transactions, and Wu clan had twenty to thirty resource points similar to it, with about ten top tier points better than it.",
      "chapters": [
        1343
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "resource-ranking",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wedding dress lake and empty origin pit are named as resource points more valuable than Blood Tide Pit.",
      "chapters": [
        1346
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "resource-ranking",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration says that in his younger days Shang Yan Fei found blood handprint Immortal Gu in Southern Border’s Blood Tide Pit.",
      "chapters": [
        2246
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
